\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1. The day The Lord God created man,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj To mark the end of creation
\par Through his divine pow'r and divine will
\par Gave names to all His creation
\par He rules over all creation
\par And the earth was his Kingdom
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. He looked for his human likelihood
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To live with and keep company
\par For one person could not live alone
\par He will need a good companion
\par One who would satisfy his choice
\par And would ever be his helper
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He made man fall into deep slumber
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj And when he was found deep in his sleep
\par He removed one of his rib bones
\par And He closed up the gap with flesh
\par That bone was formed into a female
\par She was sent to be with Adam
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  And Adam proclaimed that: Now this is
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 A bone of bones out of my flesh
\par And it is a flesh out of my flesh
\par I am a husband, she is a wife
\par They will desert father and mother
\par And be united to each other
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  Now they will then become one body
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj They will no more be two people
\par They have been united by God the Lord
\par But only death can separate them
\par What God has now joined together
\par \pard      Nobody should separate them.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

